 Every boot-keyboard interface on the bus is bound, not only the first.
 codex-vm's default topology carries TWO keyboards -- one on root port 2
 and one behind the high-speed hub on root port 4 -- and until this test
 nothing asserted that the second is reachable while the first is alive.

 `-hid-keys` routes the scripted keys through the USB HID model alone:
 no PS/2 queue, no host-side write into the key cell. `got=30` therefore
 proves a scancode travelled interrupt-IN DMA, drain and decode end to
 end, which no bed test had ever shown -- injected keys used to reach
 the guest through the PS/2 emulation whatever the USB stack did.

 The injected keys appear on the ROOT keyboard here, so the primary's
 sticky non-zero count must move and the hub peer's must stay zero: the
 peer delivers the all-zero idle reports of a keyboard nobody types on.

Section: Test

  peers-line : UsbKbd -> Text
  peers-line (k) =
    "kbd: ok=" & (if k.uk-ok then "1" else "0")
      & " peers=" & show (kbd-peers k)
      & " peer0-route=" & (if kbd-peers k > 0 then show (((kbd-peer k 0).uk-dev).ud-route) else "-")

 The wait is bounded by the RTC rather than by an iteration count: each
 pump costs several VM exits, so a count large enough to cover the key
 timeline in iterations is minutes of wall clock.

  ukm-wait : UsbKbd, Integer, Integer, Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  ukm-wait (k) (want) (prev) (secs) = act
    sc <- kbd-take k
    now <- rtc-seconds 0
    if sc == want then sc
    else if secs <= 0 then 0
    else if now < 0 then ukm-wait k want prev secs
    else if now == prev then ukm-wait k want prev secs
    else ukm-wait k want now (secs - 1)
  end

  yn : Integer -> Text
  yn (n) = if n > 0 then "Y" else "0"

  opening : [Console, Device.Port, Device.Mmio] Nothing = act
    att <- usb-attach
    let k = att.ua-kbd
    in act
      print-line-uni (peers-line k)
      s0 <- rtc-seconds 0
      got <- ukm-wait k 30 s0 8
      print-line-uni ("got=" & show got)
      print-line-uni ("primary-live=" & yn (kbd-live k) & " peer-live=" & (if kbd-peers k > 0 then yn (kbd-live (kbd-peer k 0)) else "-"))
    end
  end
